\section{Local Ollama Feasibility Note}\label{app:runtime-ollama-feasibility}
\textbf{Objective and evidence scope.} This appendix records a bounded four-episode feasibility exercise (\path{src/nesy_game/runtime_model_swap_ollama.py} and \path{scripts/run_runtime_model_swap_ollama.py}; Table~\ref{tab:artifact-directory-map}) testing whether local open-weight models served via Ollama \texttt{0.30.10} on loopback can be gated and replayed through the same deterministic planner and Godot commit boundary. All four assigned episodes were executed ($4/4$) and none reached the end-to-end quest goal ($0/4$). Because the first pilot row was executed before its plan-only receipt was written (whereas rows 2--4 wrote plan-only receipts pre-execution), these rows are reported as a descriptive feasibility exercise rather than a frozen prospective cohort, separating response-qualified eligibility ($1/4$) from goal completion ($0/4$).

\textbf{Row-by-row diagnostic interpretation (Table~\ref{tab:ollama-feasibility}).} The language model classified public utterances into typed intents while the symbolic planner selected actions across two serializations (\texttt{general\_rule} and \texttt{ontology}) of the same public facts:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Row 1 (\texttt{qwen2.5:1.5b}, \texttt{general\_rule}):} Returned 12 non-timeout responses whose response-model field matched the requested selector (\texttt{Receipts = 12/0/0}, \texttt{Eligible = yes}), but exhausted the host-call budget without a state-changing commit (\texttt{Failure code = BUDGET}, \texttt{State/replay = no-change / valid}, \texttt{Engineering status = NOT\_PASS}).
  \item \textbf{Rows 2--3 (\texttt{qwen2.5:1.5b / ontology} and \texttt{qwen2.5:0.5b / general\_rule}):} Terminated under the 30\,s response deadline, which included cold model loading with \texttt{keep\_alive=0} (\texttt{Receipts = 4/0/1} and \texttt{0/0/1}; \texttt{Failure code = TIMEOUT}). Because timeout receipts lack a response-model observation, both rows are marked \texttt{Eligible = no} and \texttt{NOT\_PASS}.
  \item \textbf{Row 4 (\texttt{qwen2.5:0.5b}, \texttt{ontology}):} Produced 1 verified receipt and 4 malformed-response receipts (\texttt{Receipts = 1/4/0}, \texttt{Failure code = REPAIR}, \texttt{Eligible = no}; raw malformed text was not retained). Crucially, the single valid repaired step committed 1 canonical state change that replayed identically in a fresh Godot process with zero model calls (\texttt{State/replay = 1 change / valid}), establishing \texttt{Engineering status = PASS} for the commit-and-replay seam despite $0/4$ quest completion.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Provenance boundary.} Across all 21 non-timeout responses, requested and served model names agreed, and Ollama model manifest/blob digests matched before and after execution. Episode record, receipt, and request hashes verify, whereas adapter/runner source bytes were not contemporaneously hash-bound into the local episode records (which retain local paths and are not externally distributed).
